-- title:
--   Geometric κ-fibre of the strict transform of the zero component
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage p`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackage.html#L43), i.e. a package of data attached to the two-chart integral model over $\mathbb{Z}$ of the full modular function field at $p$ (properness, flatness, integrality and normality of that model, rational and geometric generic curve models with their Galois compatibilities, distinguished sections, a smooth locus, and in particular a curve model `𝔛.ratModel κ` over a field $\kappa$ together with a morphism `𝔛.compZero κ` from it to the $\kappa$-fibre $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathrm{DRModel.toBase}\ p, \operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}\to\kappa))$). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $H$ be the conjunction [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) of site hypotheses (finiteness of the set of nodes, existence of oriented crossing charts on the $O$-model, étale neighbourhood data, injectivity of the node-point assignment, closedness of each node point, and the model hypotheses), summarised here. Assume further that each point $\xi_j$ lies in the open `X0` of the chart input [`V3Asm.C`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L280), namely the complement of the finitely many marked node points. The conclusion asserts the existence of a morphism $e$ from the fibre product of the composite of the closed immersion `(V3Asm.comp … (Sum.inl 1)).subschemeι` of the closed subscheme of the glued resolved model $Y$ cut out by the ideal sheaf data indexed by `Sum.inl 1` with the structure morphism [`V3Asm.toBase`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L287) $: Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$, taken along $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa) : \operatorname{Spec}\kappa \to \operatorname{Spec} O$, to `(𝔛.ratModel κ).C`, such that $e$ is an isomorphism, $e$ followed by `(𝔛.ratModel κ).toBase` is the second projection to $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, and $e$ followed by `𝔛.compZero κ` and then by the base-change map [`ModularCurve.DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`](def/ModularCurve_DRResolvedModelPackageV4.html#L24) into the $O$-fibre equals the first projection followed by that closed immersion and then by [`V3Asm.toDR`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L286) $: Y \to$ `XO p O`.
--
--   This is the field of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model package identifying the geometric special fibre over $\kappa$ of the strict transform of the zero component with the prescribed curve model over $\kappa$, compatibly with the map to $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ and with the projection to the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$. It is used in the assembly [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts), which produces the resolved model together with its étale crossing charts.
